# Files that are EXECUTED on Linux must never be checked out with CRLF: a shebang
# line ending `bash\r` is not a program, and the failure is a baffling
# "\r: command not found" rather than anything that names the real cause. The Windows
# machines in this repo run with core.autocrlf=true, so this is a live risk every time
# one of these files is edited there — pin the endings rather than rely on nobody
# noticing.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.bash    text eol=lf

# systemd unit files are parsed by systemd, not a shell, and it does not accept CRLF
# in directives either.
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer   text eol=lf

# The PowerShell side is Windows-only; leave it to git's normal handling.
